 36S  c  1986Du07 (also 1986Du11, 1987DuZU): {+36}Si activity was produced by   
 36S 2c  Al({+40}Ar,X) with E=60 MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar beam at GANIL. Fragments   
 36S 3c  were separated by the LISE spectrometer and implanted into a movable   
 36S 4c  thin photocinema foil. |b particles were detected with a plastic       
 36S 5c  scintillator and |g rays were detected with an intrinsic Ge detectors. 
 36S 6c  Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |g(t). Deduced parent T{-1/2}. No decay  
 36S 7c  scheme is given.                                                       
 36S  c  Theoretical calculations of |b decay: 1987Wa10                         
 36S  c  The decay scheme is deduced by the evaluator from |g-ray data in       
 36S 2c  1986Du07, based on the adopted level scheme and |g-ray placements.     
 36S  c  The decay scheme is considered incomplete by the evaluator, due to a   
 36S 2c  large gap of about 4 MeV between the highest possibly populated level  
 36S 3c  at E=7272 keV and Q-value=10413 keV and also due to very limited       
 36S 4c  information in 1986Du07 about this decay                               
 36S  cB IB,LOGFT$|b{+-} feeding is deduced from |g+ce intensity balance at each
 36S 2cB level. Due to incomplete decay scheme, all feeding values should be    
 36S 3cB considered upper limits and associated log {Ift} values should be      
 36S 4cB considered lower limits. However, possible unobserved transitions might
 36S 5cB not have a significant impact on those very strong branches (e.g.,     
 36S 6cB %I|b{+-}=62 to 5831 level). Feeding values with uncertainties are given
 36S 7cB under comments for reference only                                      
